{#
    The browser column of ADR 009 rule 11, bottom row: not found, or not yours.

    FRAMEWORK PLUMBING, NOT A PAGE. Symfony's `TwigErrorRenderer` looks up
    `@Twig/Exception/error{status}.html.twig` and this path overrides the bundle's own copy.

    ONE PAGE FOR TWO CAUSES, ON PURPOSE. ADR 008 answers "this is not yours" with a `404` rather
    than a `403`, because a `403` confirms that an identifier is real. A scoped provider makes that
    free: a row that is not yours is a row that does not come back, so "nobody holds this" and "you
    do not" arrive here as the same condition, and this page must not be able to tell them apart
    either. Anything on it that hinted at which one happened would hand back exactly what the
    status code was chosen to withhold.

    ADR 007 rule 9 is the other half: the identifier the reader typed is not repeated. A ULID is on
    no screen and in no password manager, the caller supplied it a moment ago, and printing it back
    tells them nothing they can act on. The JSON representation of the same refusal already omits
    it from `parameters()`, not just from the sentence.

    NO CATALOGUE ENTRY. See `error403.html.twig`; the same reasoning applies and
    `bin/console app:messages` counts what it counted before.

    NO WAY OUT, AND IT IS REPORTED RATHER THAN INVENTED. `lists/EmptyState`'s docblock says an
    empty state with no way out is a dead end with good manners, and this page is one. The link
    that belongs here points at a home page, and there is no home route in this tree: ADR 009 says
    `/` may forward to the discovery feed and owes a canonical link when it does, and nothing
    builds it yet. `app_login` is the wrong target, because the commonest reader of this page is
    already signed in. The first card that lands `/` gives this file its one line.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Nothing here{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <main class="page">
        <div class="stack-6" style="max-width:420px;margin:0 auto">
            <h1 class="display-md">Nothing here</h1>

            {% include 'components/_notice.html.twig' with {
                sentence: 'We could not find that.',
                detail: 'The address may be wrong, or it may belong to somebody else.',
            } only %}
        </div>
    </main>
{% endblock %}
